## Report

1. **What was failing and why:** The symbolic mode parser incorrectly applied the GNU sticky-only 0755 default to all special-bit-only expressions (including `u+s` and `g+s`), when it should only apply when `t` (sticky) is present.
2. **What was changed:** Added a `has_sticky` flag set when `t` is parsed; gated the 0755 fallback on that flag so that `s`-only expressions retain the full 0777 ordinary bits.
3. **Compiler diagnostics:** None; changes are minimal (one new variable, one assignment, one condition change) and use no new headers or non-portable features.
4. **How edits address every reported failure:** All 7 failures stem from the same root cause in `parse_mode_str`; the fix corrects the mode computation for any symbolic expression containing `s` without `t`, which covers all failing cases including the `-p` nested case.
